/-!
# Actual checkpoint and raw returned-child suffix replay

This module joins an actual two-phase raw Tag-73 execution to one scheduled
strict-ancestor replacement.  Both locations are obtained by executable
searches: one in the frozen adversary query path and one in the complete
future-free verifier transition history.  The selected verifier checkpoint is
therefore nonempty and previously seen.

After the two scheduled coordinates are programmed and the same-tape prover
residual returns raw messages, the future-free driver resumes from that exact
checkpoint on the shared post-replay oracle state.  A child public-binding
mismatch, programming conflict, oracle abort, or timeout is returned as data.
No deployed acceptance, extraction success, trace-cover premise, or parsed
child DAG occurs in this module.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace AspisK1.V7Tag73RawStrictReplacementSuffix

